    <p>Do not add your phone number, full home address, bank details or images of official identity documents to your public profile. Photos may reveal information about your religion or origin, so upload only what you choose to show to others.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-4">
    <h2>4. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
    <p>Unless stated otherwise, the statutory references below are to the GDPR/DSGVO.</p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Creating your account and profile, search and matching, and in-app communication</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Performance of a contract, Article 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Subscriptions and paid services</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Performance of a contract, Article 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Invoices, retention of financial records and proof of cancellation</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legal obligation, Article 6(1)(c), together with § 147 AO and § 257 HGB</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Security, prevention of fraud and fake accounts, handling reports and defending legal claims</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interests in protecting users and the platform, Article 6(1)(f); handling reports may also be based on Article 6(1)(c) and Articles 16 and 17 of the Digital Services Act (DSA)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Technical operation of the application and troubleshooting</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f); access to information on your device under § 25(2) TDDDG</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Special-category data in your profile or search preferences</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Explicit consent, Article 9(2)(a)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Interviews, videos and publication as part of paid services</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Performance of a contract, Article 6(1)(b); your separate consent for publication, Article 6(1)(a) together with §§ 22 and 23 KUG, and Article 9(2)(a) for any special-category data</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Receiving VIP suggestions</td><td data-label="Legal basis">Your consent, Article 6(1)(a)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>Our legitimate interest is to operate a secure platform, free from fraud and fake accounts, and to establish and defend our rights in the event of a dispute.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-5">
    <h2>5. Special-category personal data</h2>
    <p>Providing information about religion, racial or ethnic origin, or health is optional. We process this information only with your explicit consent under Article 9(2)(a), and only to display it on your profile and help you search for a partner. You can use Wesal without providing this information. You can delete it or withdraw your consent at any time through the relevant settings. It is not published outside the application unless you separately and expressly approve the exact content to be published.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-6">
    <h2>6. Search and matching</h2>
    <p>Wesal uses the information in your profile to display search results and suggestions according to the criteria you select, such as age, country and personal preferences. These suggestions are an aid only. No automated decision is made that produces legal effects concerning you or similarly significantly affects you within the meaning of Article 22 GDPR, and we do not create profiles for advertising purposes.</p>
    <p>With paid plans, a member can see who has visited their profile. Your visit may therefore be shown to a member with an eligible paid plan. This processing is necessary to perform the contract under Article 6(1)(b).</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-7">
    <h2>7. Paid services involving our team</h2>
    <p>For some services, members of our team work with your data. Access is limited to people assigned to the service, only to the extent necessary, and they are bound by written confidentiality obligations.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>VIP plan – interview and publication:</strong> We interview you, prepare text or a video about you, publish it and renew the publication once a month for three months, as described in section 8. The interview takes place at our office or through a call on WhatsApp, TikTok or Facebook, as you choose. When one of these applications is used, its operator processes call data under its own privacy policy (see section 15).</li>
        <li><strong>VIP plan – manual search:</strong> Our team searches the Wesal database for members who may be suitable and sends them a link to your profile inside the application. Suggestions are sent only to members who have enabled receiving them. They are marked “VIP suggestion” and can be disabled in settings. We do not transfer your special-category data to another user except as allowed by your profile settings.</li>
        <li><strong>One-time publication service:</strong> You complete a form. We create one video and publish it once as described in section 8, without an interview or manual search.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-8">
    <h2>8. Publication outside the application</h2>
    <p>We do not publish anything about you outside the application because you registered or purchased an ordinary subscription. External publication takes place only after you purchase a publication service, review the final text or video, and approve it using a separate consent box.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>The post contains only what you approved, together with a link to your Wesal profile. That link is accessible only to registered users aged 18 or over.</li>
        <li>We do not publish your full legal name, phone number, address, external social-media accounts or identity documents unless you expressly consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Platforms:</strong> TikTok and Facebook. Anyone may be able to view the post and others may copy it. These platforms process the content under their own policies.</li>
        <li>Paid content is labelled as commercial content or advertising.</li>
        <li>We delete posts and interview materials from our accounts within six months, or earlier if you request it.</li>
        <li>You may withdraw your publication consent at any time by contacting Wesal management, support or email. We then remove the post from our accounts within three days and disable the link. We cannot remove copies already saved by other people. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of publication before the withdrawal.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-9">
    <h2>9. Messages between users</h2>
    <p>We process messages to provide communication inside the application. Our team does not routinely read private messages. If a message is reported, we review only the material submitted by the reporting person with the report, to the extent necessary to investigate, or where required by law. Messages are encrypted in transit.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-10">
    <h2>10. Security and reports</h2>
    <p>We process the data necessary to detect fake accounts, impersonation and fraud. If there are reasonable security concerns, we may request additional verification using proof of identity. The document is used only for verification and is deleted after verification is complete.</p>
    <p>After reviewing a report, we may warn a user, remove content, restrict an account or close it. We inform the affected user of the decision and its reason, and inform the reporting person of the outcome, in accordance with Articles 16 and 17 DSA. Our content-review process is described in the Terms of Use.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-11">
    <h2>11. Technical data and notifications</h2>
    <p>When you use the application or website, technical data is recorded, including your IP address, time of access, device, operating system, app version and error logs. This is necessary to operate and protect the service. Server logs are deleted after 90 days.</p>
    <p>We send notifications about messages, interactions, your account, security and subscriptions. You can disable notifications in your device settings. We do not send promotional emails unless you consent or the conditions in § 7(3) UWG are met. You can opt out at any time.</p>
    <p>We do not use your precise geographic location. If we introduce a feature that requires it, we will ask for your permission first.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-12">
    <h2>12. Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>We use only technologies that are strictly necessary to operate the application and website, such as maintaining your login session and remembering your language (§ 25(2) TDDDG). We do not use analytics or marketing services unless and until they are activated in accordance with the applicable consent requirements. Any service that requires consent will operate only after you have given that consent.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-13">
    <h2>13. Payments</h2>
    <p>Payments are processed through Stripe Payments Europe Ltd., 1 Grand Canal Street Lower, Dublin 2, Ireland. Wesal does not store complete payment-card details on its servers. The payment provider also processes payment data under its own responsibility, for example to prevent fraud and meet banking obligations, in accordance with its own privacy policy.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-14">
    <h2>14. Recipients of personal data</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal data. Technical service providers act on our instructions under data-processing agreements in accordance with Article 28 GDPR. The following recipients receive data only to the extent necessary:</p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Recipient</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">Hostinger</td><td data-label="Purpose">Website, server and database hosting</td><td data-label="Location">Germany</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">Email service for the wesalsyria.com domain</td><td data-label="Purpose">Account and confirmation emails</td><td data-label="Location">Germany</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google)</td><td data-label="Purpose">Delivery of push notifications</td><td data-label="Location">European Union, with possible transfers to the United States (section 15)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">Stripe</td><td data-label="Purpose">Payment processing</td><td data-label="Location">Ireland, with possible transfers to the United States (section 15)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">TikTok and Facebook</td><td data-label="Purpose">Publication only with your consent (section 8)</td><td data-label="Location">Ireland, with possible transfers outside the European Union (section 15)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Recipient">Other users</td><td data-label="Purpose">Viewing your profile according to the information you chose to provide</td><td data-label="Location">Within Wesal</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>We do not use a separate crash-reporting service. We provide data to public authorities only when required by law.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-15">
    <h2>15. Storage location and transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>We store your data on servers in the European Union and European Economic Area. Some providers mentioned in section 14 (Google for Firebase, Stripe, social-media platforms and WhatsApp when used for an interview) may transfer data to countries outside the European Union, such as the United States. Such transfers take place only with appropriate safeguards under Articles 45 or 46 GDPR: an adequacy decision under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework for companies certified under that framework, or otherwise the European Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses. You may request a copy of the relevant safeguards by email.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-16">
    <h2>16. How long we retain data</h2>
    <p>We retain personal data only for as long as it is necessary for the relevant purpose, after which it is deleted or anonymised.</p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Retention period</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Account, profile and photos</td><td data-label="Retention period">While the account exists, then deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Messages in a conversation involving a deleted account</td><td data-label="Retention period">The conversation is hidden when the account is deleted. Its messages and deleted conversation record are permanently removed by the scheduled cleanup after 30 days.</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Reports and security records</td><td data-label="Retention period">12 months after a report is closed, and longer only where a dispute remains ongoing</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Identity-verification document</td><td data-label="Retention period">Deleted after verification is complete</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Server logs</td><td data-label="Retention period">90 days</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Interview materials, videos and publications</td><td data-label="Retention period">Up to six months, or until you request deletion or withdraw consent; in the latter case, removal from our accounts takes place within three days</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Consent records</td><td data-label="Retention period">Three years after the consent ends, to demonstrate the consent (general limitation period under § 195 BGB)</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Invoices and accounting vouchers</td><td data-label="Retention period">Eight years under § 147 AO and § 257 HGB</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Books, inventories and annual accounts</td><td data-label="Retention period">Ten years under § 147 AO and § 257 HGB</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Other tax-relevant business records and correspondence</td><td data-label="Retention period">Six years where the statutory six-year period applies under § 147 AO and § 257 HGB</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Data">Contract and cancellation records</td><td data-label="Retention period">Three years after the end of the contract, unless a longer statutory retention obligation applies</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>Statutory accounting and tax-retention periods generally begin at the end of the calendar year in which the relevant record was created or the last entry was made. Where a statutory suspension or extension applies, the records are retained for the period required by law.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-17">
    <h2>17. Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>You can delete your account at any time using the delete-account option in the account settings in the application, through <a href="https://www.wesalsyria.com/delete-account" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.wesalsyria.com/delete-account</a>, or by contacting us by email. After deletion, your profile is immediately hidden from other users and publication links to it are disabled. We retain only the information required by law or necessary to establish or defend legal claims, for the periods described in section 16. When your account is deleted, all plans associated with it end and no further payment is taken.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-18">
    <h2>18. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR, you have the following rights. You may exercise them free of charge by emailing <a href="mailto:wesalsyrien@gmail.com">wesalsyrien@gmail.com</a>. We respond within one month.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Access to the personal data we hold about you and a copy of that data (Article 15)</li>
        <li>Correction of inaccurate data (Article 16)</li>
        <li>Erasure of data (Article 17)</li>
        <li>Restriction of processing (Article 18)</li>
        <li>Data portability in a machine-readable format (Article 20)</li>
        <li>Withdrawal of consent at any time, as easily as it was given; withdrawal does not affect processing carried out before it (Article 7(3))</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-19">
    <h2>19. Right to object</h2>
    <p>At any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation, you may object to processing based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (Article 21(1)). We will then stop processing unless we demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests, or the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims. You may also object at any time to the use of your data for direct marketing (Article 21(2)). Send your objection to <a href="mailto:wesalsyrien@gmail.com">wesalsyrien@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-20">
    <h2>20. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
    <p>You may lodge a complaint with any data-protection supervisory authority, particularly in the country where you live or work (Article 77 GDPR). The authority responsible for us is:</p>
    <p><strong>Die Sächsische Datenschutz- und Transparenzbeauftragte</strong></p>
    <p>Devrientstraße 5, 01067 Dresden, Germany</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-21">
    <h2>21. Age requirement</h2>
    <p>Wesal is intended only for people aged 18 or over. When registering, you confirm that you are at least 18 years old. If we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we delete the account and its data immediately, subject to any legal obligations.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-22">
    <h2>22. Data security</h2>
    <p>We take appropriate technical and organisational measures under Article 32 GDPR, including encryption during transmission (TLS), access controls and backups. No electronic system can be guaranteed to be 100% secure.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="privacy-23">
    <h2>23. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We update this policy when our services, providers or applicable law change. We publish the updated version with its date and notify you inside the application of material changes. We request fresh consent whenever a new purpose requires it.</p>
</section>

